appened-w6alse1gi","summary":"A walkthrough of using Ghost (ghost.build), a free MCP-compatible database tool, with Claude Code for AI-agent-driven database workflows. The tool allows spinning up, forking, and discarding PostgreSQL databases instantly and for free, making it safe for AI agents to experiment without risking production data. Demos include creating databases with seeded data, building a Next.js dashboard, parallel query optimization across three forked databases using different strategies (indexes, materialized views, denormalized tables), and running 10 parallel database forks to test data migration/cleanup strategies before applying the best one to the base database.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vJBAzdOACD8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T13:01:40.000Z"},{"id":"FXu776Nel","title":"Nine stage roadmap for building apps with AI in 2026","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xEr0hRbK_Xo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-make-an-app-with-ai---9-steps-fxu776nel","summary":"A nine-stage roadmap for building apps with AI, covering everything from defining what to build and planning a tech stack, to choosing between no-code platforms (Lovable, Bolt) and AI coding tools (Cursor, Claude Code), setting up environments with MCP servers, selecting AI models within budget, building an MVP incrementally, implementing CI/CD with automated testing, and deploying with monitoring and logging. Emphasizes structured process over ad-hoc vibe coding to avoid scope creep and maintainability issues.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/xEr0hRbK_Xo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T14:01:29.000Z"},{"id":"pg3bvossy","title":"How to configure local LLM models in OpenClaw using Ollama","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UVUzdRLuAoA","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/watch-till-the-end--pg3bvossy","summary":"A walkthrough of configuring OpenClaw to run local LLM models (specifically Gemma 4 via Ollama) on a local machine. The process involves running 'openclaw configure', selecting a model, choosing local-only mode, and restarting the gateway to make the models available within OpenClaw.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/UVUzdRLuAoA/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T10:39:53.000Z"},{"id":"jW7Pk4rjg","title":"How to learn Python for AI without getting stuck in tutorial hell","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DZIymFrEXik","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/do-this-instead-of-watching-endless-tutorials-how-to-learn-python-for-ai-jw7pk4rjg","summary":"A practical guide for beginners who want to learn Python specifically for AI development, focused on escaping 'tutorial hell'. The approach covers the minimal Python subset needed (variables, functions, lists, dicts, JSON, file I/O, pip), then immediately building projects: a CLI chatbot, a document Q&A tool using RAG, and an AI agent with tool-calling. Emphasizes active coding over passive watching, recommends a 1:1 ratio of learning to building, and warns against the 'one more course' trap. DataCamp is recommended as a sponsor with specific tracks for Python fundamentals and AI engineering.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/DZIymFrEXik/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-26T14:00:18.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["mentaloutlaw","thevimeagen","aidotengineer","bytegrad","lauriewired"],"opposite_handles":["horde","watercooler","dailydevworld","on_leuwcq","devtools"],"similar":[{"id":"mentaloutlaw","handle":"mentaloutlaw","name":"Mental Outlaw","is_squad":false,"x":-6.8882,"y":-9.6139,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":234,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s---3xRV5E---/f_auto/v1712315214/logos/mentaloutlaw","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":2.151185,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.00641,"avg_read_time":12.188034,"tag_diversity":0.521368},"top_tags_